{"parentUuid":"8deb1325-96c3-45f3-a877-976b2da42726","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgadT92L42dbmTuG4Qr7X","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The push of `4855dca` is still uploading checkpoints. Writing the plan update while it runs."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":501,"cache_read_input_tokens":628503,"output_tokens":2039,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":501,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2039,"cache_read_input_tokens":628503,"cache_creation_input_tokens":501,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":501},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"918919c9-00dc-4720-9f47-00263f9e0a35","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgadT8dmcNHE3qG2g45nf","type":"assistant","uuid":"57403960-eb1d-45f5-9d04-9b0f04c3e632","timestamp":"2026-10-31T16:27:30.673Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"pure-pondering-goose"}
{"parentUuid":"57403960-eb1d-45f5-9d04-9b0f04c3e632","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgadT92L42dbmTuG4Qr7X","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Sqc33WtbaoFpwreLBRoPeR","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\n# D21 row\na=\"| D21 | The audit record is a hash chain with one writer. Each entry carries the hash of the one before it, and verification walks the chain. | Any change to a past entry breaks the chain, so the record is tamper-evident. It cannot stop a change; it shows one. |\"\nb=\"| D21 | The audit record is a hash chain with one writer. Each entry carries an HMAC-SHA256 of its fields and the entry before it, keyed with a secret kept in the macOS Keychain, not in the record, and verification walks the chain. | Any change to a past entry breaks the chain, and whoever can edit the database cannot recompute it without the Keychain key. It still cannot stop a change, or detect entries cut from the end; a remote append-only copy (§10) closes that, later. |\"\nassert s.count(a)==1; s=s.replace(a,b)\ni=s.index(\"| A5 | in progress |\"); j=s.index(\"\\n\",i)\nrow=\"\"\"| A5 | done | The gate, the ladders and the audit chain in `bastion-core` (def679b); the governance tables, the hook and the owner's commands (a509bb1); held calls and the Governance page (b4f2704). First live exit on `j4825765c` (ee4435e): a plan's write held, Allow once ran exactly it, Refuse reached the agent, `keep-tests` passed a `git rm` at checked and refused it at enforced, and verification failed after one byte of entry 20 changed. Then, from what that exit found: the review page freeze (513da6c); a keyed chain, its writer's state with a 5 s limit per write, and export (d0d3a27); charter constraints and repository hooks from `.claude/settings.json` (37a4b8e); a `tests-kept` constraint on the review diff (c7e992b); Stop during a busy turn and a single send-back (2b9afae); the add form and each constraint's history (4855dca). 45 core tests, 49 app tests, 2 view tests. Second live exit (2026-10-31) on `j3e0ca30c`, with a charter in `demo-a` (deny `Bash(git push:*)`, a PreToolUse hook that refuses `rm`, a Stop hook that runs pytest): the job page showed the charter, its rule and every hook run; the hook passed 12 calls with exit 0 and refused `rm -f /work/repo/notes.txt` with exit 2 and its own message; the Stop hook ran pytest after each build; with `tests-kept` enforced, a build that dropped `test_add` went back to build with the rule, and at checked the same finding waited for the owner. On the Governance page, the form added `no-curl` (entry 333), History listed `tests-kept`'s promotion and demotion, the chain verified 332 and then 335 entries under the Keychain key, and Export wrote 335 entries and `{\"verified\":true}`. Not run live: the `git push` deny rule (the agent read it in its brief and never made the call; the core and gate tests cover it), and a stalled audit (the unit test covers it). |\"\"\"\ns=s[:i]+row+s[j:]\ns=s.replace(\"| A6 to A13 | — | — |\",\"| A6 | next | — |\\n| A7 to A13 | — | — |\") if \"| A6 to A13 | — | — |\" in s else s\n# findings\ns=s.replace(\"**What A5 found so far:**\",\"**What A5 found:**\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"- Not fixed: typing a comma into the review note box while a wide diff is on\n  the page spins the webview at 100% CPU. The same comma in the Jobs search\n  box is fine. The page also scrolls sideways at review, so a layout loop is\n  the first suspect.\"\"\",\"\"\"- Typing a comma into the review note froze the webview at 100% CPU. A\n  sample showed the main thread answering `AXVisibleCharacterRange`, which\n  WebKit measures across the whole page; macOS text checking asks for it after\n  punctuation. `spellcheck=\"false\"` on the note boxes fixed it. The layout was\n  not the cause, though the page did scroll sideways, which is also fixed.\"\"\")\ns=s.rstrip(\"\\n\")+\"\"\"\n- A rule on a call cannot see a test deleted by rewriting its file. A\n  constraint on the review diff (`tests-kept`) can. An enforced finding sends\n  the work back once: live, eight builds in a row restored `test_add` under a\n  new name until the job was stopped.\n- Every hook run pushes a change, and the job page rebuilt its header on each\n  one, so a click on Stop during a busy turn was lost. Stop now sits outside\n  the part that re-renders.\n- The repository's charter is read at each turn start. A job that has not\n  started a turn since the app started shows no charter yet.\n- `sandbox::exec` takes `cmd` and `args` as well as `argv`; the gate reads\n  all three, or a rule on a command line sees nothing.\n- An agent that reads a deny rule in its brief does not try the call, so the\n  gate never sees it. A rule told is often a rule obeyed.\n- The page shifts under a click when it reloads, and a mis-aimed click\n  promoted a grant during the exit. The audit showed the promotion and the\n  demotion that undid it. Two-step confirmation on a promotion is worth\n  considering in A7.\n- Trunk's file watcher died after the disk filled, and a timestamp-only touch\n  does not trigger a rebuild. Restart `cargo tauri dev` after a full disk.\n\"\"\"\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"^| A5 \\|^| A6 \\|^| A7\" PLAN.md | cut -c1-80","description":"Close A5 in the plan with its evidence"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":501,"cache_read_input_tokens":628503,"output_tokens":2039,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":501,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2039,"cache_read_input_tokens":628503,"cache_creation_input_tokens":501,"cac