{"parentUuid":"27ee08d5-67b6-48bb-ae12-8cd56da1d1cc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgadVqZgj27PodAfjRHsP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":397,"cache_read_input_tokens":632200,"output_tokens":1404,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":133},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":397,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1404,"cache_read_input_tokens":632200,"cache_creation_input_tokens":397,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":397},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"48fb7cd3-895b-48b7-a727-28ab187f1966","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgadVqD7B6cuaMUvaxPPe","type":"assistant","uuid":"ac9219cd-d869-4756-8883-30c129c2ae56","timestamp":"2026-10-31T16:28:14.342Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"pure-pondering-goose"}
{"parentUuid":"ac9219cd-d869-4756-8883-30c129c2ae56","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgadVqZgj27PodAfjRHsP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The comma freeze is fixed, and A5 is closed in `PLAN.md` with the evidence from a second live exit. The audit chain now stays local as you asked: it is keyed with a secret held in your macOS Keychain. CI passed on every push through `2b9afae`. `4855dca` is still running, and `866b79c` (the plan update) is still pushing.\n\n**Comma freeze:** the cause was macOS text checking, not our code. After a comma, it asks WebKit for the visible text range, and WebKit walks the whole review page to answer. With `spellcheck=\"false\"` on the two note boxes, the freeze reproduced three times before the change and not once after (`513da6c`). The same commit fixes the page scrolling sideways at review.\n\n**Tamper-resistant audit (local):** each entry's hash is now an HMAC-SHA256 keyed with a secret in the Keychain (service `bastion-audit`), not in the database (`d0d3a27`). Someone who edits the database can no longer recompute the chain without that key. It still can't stop a change, or notice entries cut off the end; a remote copy will close that later. If the app can't read the key, the gate refuses every call. Export writes the chain plus a closing line that says whether it verified.\n\n**The rest of A5:**\n- **Charter rules:** the repository's `.claude/settings.json` deny and ask lists become constraints. Its PreToolUse hooks run in the job's VM before a matching call, and exit 2 refuses the call. Its Stop hooks run after each build (`37a4b8e`).\n- **No charter:** the job page shows the charter, its rules and every hook run, or says the job runs on your defaults.\n- **Deleted tests:** a new constraint, `tests-kept`, checks the review diff for tests that were removed (`c7e992b`). Rules on calls couldn't catch this, because the agent deleted tests by rewriting the test file.\n- **Add and history:** the Governance page can now add a constraint and show each constraint's history (`4855dca`).\n\n**Second live exit (job `j3e0ca30c`, with a charter in `demo-a`):**\n- The repository's hook passed 12 calls and refused `rm -f /work/repo/notes.txt` with its own message.\n- The Stop hook ran pytest after each build.\n- With `tests-kept` enforced, a build that dropped `test_add` was sent back. At checked, the same finding waited for me instead.\n- The form added `no-curl`, and History showed `tests-kept`'s promotion and demotion.\n- The chain verified 335 entries under the Keychain key, and Export wrote them with `{\"verified\":true}`.\n\n**Bugs the exit found, fixed in `2b9afae`:**\n- **Stop didn't respond during a busy turn.** Each hook run refreshed the page and replaced the Stop button mid-click. Stop no longer re-renders.\n- **The send-back looped.** Each build put `test_add` back under a new name, so the rule fired again, eight builds in a row until I stopped the job. A finding now sends the work back only once; if it repeats, the job waits for you.\n\n**Not run live:**\n- **The `git push` deny rule.** The agent read the rule in its brief and never made the call. Unit tests cover it.\n- **A stalled audit.** A unit test covers it.\n\n**Things to check:**\n- One of my clicks missed and promoted Plan · `sandbox::fs::write` from ask to allowed. I demoted it straight back; the audit shows both, as entries 334 and 335.\n- `no-curl` is a test constraint at told. Keep or demote it as you like.\n- `demo-a` now carries my test charter (commit `d6227b2`).\n- The earlier security issue is still open: worker VMs receive your whole shell environment, secrets included. A9 should fix it.\n\nA6 (A/B evals) is next."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":397,"cache_read_input_tokens":632200,"output_tokens":1404,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":133},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":397,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1404,"cache_read_input_tokens":632200,"cache_creation_input_tokens":397,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":397},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"48fb7cd3-895b-48b7-a727-28ab187f1966","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgadVqD7B6cuaMUvaxPPe","type":"assistant","uuid":"d5a1cd93-85ce-498a-bd71-82592329400c","timestamp":"2026-10-31T16:28:19.339Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"pure-pondering-goose"}
