{"parentUuid":"20adc4d2-40c0-4519-8a2f-8190f1c03428","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"32608f53-cbf4-44d8-b1c2-0e0d5ddd2b9e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011LyU6QZBUq6hcNkc2SMaB2","type":"tool_result","content":"#### A6 — A/B evals (L)\n\n**Goal:** the owner sees what a change to the harness does before keeping it\n(D22).\n\n- An eval runs a set of requests against fixed workspace snapshots under two\n  harness configurations, A and B. A configuration is the set of constraints\n  and capabilities with their ladder positions, the model per stage, and the\n  pipeline.\n- Each run records its outcome per request: landed or not, turns, refusals,\n  checkpoint decisions, time and cost, plus a judge's grade.\n- The Evals page shows the difference between A and B per request and in\n  total, and links each difference to the hook decisions behind it.\n- A promotion or demotion can be proposed with its eval attached, and the\n  audit records the eval the owner acted on.\n\n**Exit, live:** an eval of three requests under A (a constraint told) and B\n(the same constraint enforced) shows a difference in refusals, and the\ndifference links to the refused calls.\n\n#### A7 — Settings and integrations (L)\n117:| D22 | An eval compares two harness configurations on the same requests and the same workspace snapshots, and reports the difference with the hook decisions behind it. | A promotion or demotion comes with evidence, not a guess. |\n450:(D22).\n7:tamper-evident audit record, and A/B evals that show what a change to the\n34:  recorded decision the owner can back with an eval.\n70:10. Every constraint and capability is a hook decision, so an eval of two\n115:| D20 | Every constraint and capability is enforced in a harness hook, and its ladder position is data. A turn's behavior changes only through those hooks a\n117:| D22 | An eval compares two harness configurations on the same requests and the same workspace snapshots, and reports the difference with the hook decision\n171:| A/B evals | app: `bastion-core` compares; runs are jobs | `eval`, `judge` (stock) | A6 |\n295:| Evals: grade and backtest | A/B evals of harness configurations | A6 |\n447:#### A6 — A/B evals (L)\n452:- An eval runs a set of requests against fixed workspace snapshots under two\n458:- The Evals page shows the difference between A and B per request and in\n460:- A promotion or demotion can be proposed with its eval attached, and the\n461:  audit records the eval the owner acted on.\n463:**Exit, live:** an eval of three requests under A (a constraint told) and B\n534:- Proposals: each comes with an A/B eval (A6). Accept or reject it; an\n539:**Exit, live:** a job's surprise becomes a proposal with its eval, the owner","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"7551eef2-e765-43de-90e7-b0711e1b5669","timestamp":"2026-10-31T16:28:48.146Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"#### A6 — A/B evals (L)\n\n**Goal:** the owner sees what a change to the harness does before keeping it\n(D22).\n\n- An eval runs a set of requests against fixed workspace snapshots under two\n  harness configurations, A and B. A configuration is the set of constraints\n  and capabilities with their ladder positions, the model per stage, and the\n  pipeline.\n- Each run records its outcome per request: landed or not, turns, refusals,\n  checkpoint decisions, time and cost, plus a judge's grade.\n- The Evals page shows the difference between A and B per request and in\n  total, and links each difference to the hook decisions behind it.\n- A promotion or demotion can be proposed with its eval attached, and the\n  audit records the eval the owner acted on.\n\n**Exit, live:** an eval of three requests under A (a constraint told) and B\n(the same constraint enforced) shows a difference in refusals, and the\ndifference links to the refused calls.\n\n#### A7 — Settings and integrations (L)\n117:| D22 | An eval compares two harness configurations on the same requests and the same workspace sn