{"parentUuid":"b0d6ae03-28a5-4989-a16a-cfd71cff603b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"32608f53-cbf4-44d8-b1c2-0e0d5ddd2b9e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UJd3CER3pKHn4uYTEf7DEX","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```shell\ncd /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion && cat > /tmp/ls_fn.rs 2>/dev/null; mkdir -p crates/bastion-spikes/examples && cat > crates/bastion-spikes/examples/fns.rs <<'EOF'\nuse bastion_spikes::{call_default, connect};\nuse serde_json::json;\n#[tokio::main]\nasync fn main() {\n    let prefix = std::env::args().nth(1).unwrap_or_default();\n    let iii = connect(\"spike-fns\");\n    let all = call_default(&iii, \"engine::functions::list\", json!({}), 10_000).await.expect(\"list\");\n    for f in all[\"functions\"].as_array().into_iter().flatten().filter(|f| f[\"function_id\"].as_str().unwrap_or(\"\").starts_with(&prefix)) {\n        println!(\"{} :: {}\", f[\"function_id\"], f[\"description\"].as_str().unwrap_or(\"\").chars().take(300).collect::<String>());\n    }\n    std::process::exit(0);\n}\nEOF\nRUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN=1.97.0 cargo run -q -p bastion-spikes --example fns -- judge 2>&1 | tail -20; RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN=1.97.0 cargo run -q -p bastion-spikes --example fns -- eval 2>&1 | tail -20\n```\n\n\"judge::cancel\" :: Signal cancellation of an active evaluation or model listing started by the calling worker through the same provider. Returns whether a signal was accepted; does not roll back provider work.\n\"judge::evaluate\" :: Evaluate Noul, Choice and Score questions against arbitrary JSON state through the selected judge-<provider> worker. Results are atomic; stats retain known accepted usage. No credentials are accepted in the request.\n\"judge::mentions::resolve\" :: Resolve @<name>(id=\"…\") chat mentions (found in `text`, or listed) through the workers that provide them: each one's status, one-line summary and the call that returns its full details.\n\"eval::analyze-session\" :: Analyze the latest definitive turn of a finished root Harness session. Returns the existing analysis of that turn unless reanalyze is true; reanalysis needs the previous analysis to be terminal. Works while automatic observation is paused.\n\"eval::attach-validation\" :: Link a baseline and a candidate E2E execution (read through e2e::dashboard::execution-get) to one suggestion of a terminal analysis. The link records report availability and, when the suggestion's scenario is known, the evidence computed from the runs; it is not a verdict and starts no campaign.\n\"eval::cancel\" :: Cancel an analysis: signals its Jev call and stops its investigation session. Never touches the observed session or the captured evidence.\n\"eval::config\" :: Read the monitor configuration (null until configured), whether the harness::turn-completed observation trigger was requested, the latest rejection (capacity or daily cost cap), the day's known investigation cost against the cap with what one analysis has cost, and, with check_providers, whether the\n\"eval::configure\" :: Choose the Harness model/provider the session monitor uses for investigations and enable or pause automatic observation. A new selection is checked against router::models::list; credentials stay in the providers and are never accepted here. An optional code_repository (an absolute directory on this \n\"eval::delete\" :: Delete a terminal analysis and its stored previews. The turn stays marked as analyzed until retention, so it is not re-admitted automatically.\n\"eval::list\" :: List recent monitor analyses as compact records, newest first, without evidence; observation_key keeps only the analyses of one observed turn.\n\"eval::recurrence\" :: For a suggestion marked shipped with its version, how often its patterns were found per analysis on Harness versions before it against from it on. Analyses without a semantic Harness version are left out and counted.\n\"eval::reproduce\" :: Replay the decision point of a suggestion: rebuild the request the model received at that step of the observed turn (optionally with edits that stand for the proposed change), sample the next reply N times (default 20) without running any function, and read the suggestion's signal in each reply. Spe\n\"eval::result\" :: Read an analysis with its captured evidence, deterministic diagnostics, Jev triage, suggestions, the monitor's own consumption and linked E2E executions, or null. A completed analysis is not a validated improvement.\n\"eval::review\" :: Record what a person decided about a suggestion of a terminal analysis: move its lifecycle (new, accepted, in_progress, shipped, rejected, duplicate), register the criterion a validation is judged by, or record a verdict. A verdict of validated_improvement is refused unless the criterion was registe\n\"eval::reviews\" :: List the stored suggestion reviews (lifecycle, criterion, run, evidence, verdict) and, per analysis with suggestions, how many sit at each lifecycle status.\n\"eval::start-validation\" :: Explicitly start a baseline and a candidate E2E execution for one suggestion. Both commits (candidate_ref, and baseline_ref or the merge base with origin/main) are resolved with git in the configured code_repository and must be on a remote branch; each stack is the E2E's `harness` template with only\n\"eval::status\" :: Read one analysis record (status, counters, failure stage) or null.\n"}]}]},"uuid":"30e63f43-032d-4b9f-bb2d-f6edd294735a","timestamp":"2026-10-31T16:29:37.190Z","toolUseResult":[{"type":"text","text":"```shell\ncd /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion && cat > /tmp/ls_fn.rs 2>/dev/null; mkdir -p crates/bastion-spikes/examples && cat > crates/bastion-spikes/examples/fns.rs <<'EOF'\nuse bastion_spikes::{call_default, connect};\nuse serde_json::json;\n#[tokio::main]\nasync fn main() {\n    let prefix = std::env::args().nth(1).unwrap_or_default();\n    let iii = connect(\"spike-fns\");\n    let all = call_default(&iii, \"engine::functions::list\", json!({}), 10_000).await.expect(\"list\");\n    for f in all[\"functions\"].as_array().into_iter().flatten().filter(|f| f[\"function_id\"].as_str().unwrap_or(\"\").starts_with(&prefix)) {\n        println!(\"{} :: {}\", f[\"function_id\"], f[\"description\"].as_str().unwrap_or(\"\").chars().take(300).collect::<String>());\n    }\n    std::process::exit(0);\n}\nEOF\nRUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN=1.97.0 cargo run -q -p bastion-spikes --example fns -- judge 2>&1 | tail -20; RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN=1.97.0 cargo run -q -p bastion-spikes --example fns -- eval 2>&1 | tail -20\n```\n\n\"judge::cancel\" :: Signal cancellation of an active evaluation or model listing started by the calling worker through the same provider. Returns whether a signal was accepted; does not roll back provider work.\n\"judge::evaluate\" :: Evaluate Noul, Choice and Score questions against arbitrary JSON state through the selected judge-<provider> worker. Results are atomic; stats retain known accepted usage. No credentials are accepted in the request.\n\"judge::mentions::resolve\" :: Resolve @<name>(id=\"…\") chat mentions (found in `text`, or listed) through the workers that provide them: each one's status, one-line summary and the call that returns its full details.\n\"eval::analyze-session\" :: Analyze the latest definitive turn of a finished root Harness session. Returns the existing analysis of that turn unless reanalyze is true; reanalysis needs the previous analysis to be terminal. Works while automatic observation is paused.\n\"eval::attach-validation\" :: Link a baseline and a candidate E2E execution (read through e2e::dashboard::execution-get) to one suggestion of a terminal analysis. The link records report availability and, when the suggestion's scenario is known, the evidence computed from the runs; it is not a verdict and starts no campaign.\n\"eval::cancel\" :: Cancel an analysis: signals its Jev call and stops its investigation session. Never touches the observed session or the captured evidence.\n\"eval::config\" :: Read the monitor configuration (null until configured), whether the harness::turn-completed observation trigger was requested, the latest rejection (capacity or daily cost cap), the day's known investigation cost against the cap with what one analysis has cost, and, with check_providers, whether the\n\"eval::configure\" :: Choose the Harness model/provider the session monitor uses for investigations and enable or pause automatic observation. A new selection is checked against router::models::list; credentials stay in the providers and are never accepted here. An optional code_repository (an absolute directory on this \n\"eval::delete\" :: Delete a terminal analysis and its stored previews. The turn stays marked as analyzed until retention, so it is not re-admitted automatically.\n\"eval::list\" :: List recent monitor analyses as compact records, newest first, without evidence; observation_key keeps only the analyses of one observed turn.\n\"eval::recurrence\" :: For a suggestion marked shipped with its version, how often its patterns were found per analysis on Harness versions before it against from it on. Analyses without a semantic Harness version are left out and counted.\n\"eval::reproduce\" :: Replay the decision point of a suggestion: rebuild the request the model received at that step of the observed turn (optionally with edits that stand for the proposed change), sample the next reply N times (default 20) without running any function, and read the suggestion's signal in each reply. Spe\n\"eval::result\" :: Read an analysis with its captured evidence, deterministic diagnostics, Jev triage, suggestions, the monitor's own consumption and linked E2E executions, or null. A completed analysis is not a validated improvement.\n\"eval::review\" :: Record what a person decided about a suggestion of a terminal analysis: move its lifecycle (new, accepted, in_progress, shipped, rejected, duplicate), register the criterion a validation is judged by, or record a verdict. A verdict of validated_improvement is refused unless the criterion was registe\n\"eval::reviews\" :: List the stored suggestion reviews (lifecycle, criterion, run, evidence, verdict) and, per analysis with suggestions, how many sit at each lifecycle status.\n\"eval::start-validation\" :: Explicitly start a baseline and a candidate E2E execution for one suggestion. Both commits (candidate_ref, and baseline_ref or the merge base with origin/main) are resolved with git in the configured code_repository and must be on a remote branch; each stack is the E2E's `harness` template with only\n\"eval::status\" :: Read one analysis record (status, counters, failure stage) or null.\n"}],"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"84b4b1c8-5a42-49f6-ae1c-3bb275605b1f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b0d6ae03-28a5-4989-a16a-cfd71cff603b","session_id":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"pure-pondering-goose"}
