{"parentUuid":"e8eaf1e4-4ad5-49c0-ae99-973ec7a4d4c8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"32608f53-cbf4-44d8-b1c2-0e0d5ddd2b9e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ht5nN9eYss3sC5S7PRepwc","type":"tool_result","content":"\"approval::on-turn-completed\" :: Internal: harness::turn-completed handler (purge the turn's pending records).\n\"configuration::set\" :: Replace the active configuration and notify consumers. flush=true (default) validates and persists the complete value for a registered id. flush=false updates memory only and m\n\"eval::config\" :: Read the monitor configuration (null until configured), whether the harness::turn-completed observation trigger was requested, the latest rejection (capacity or daily cost cap), the \n\"eval::result\" :: Read an analysis with its captured evidence, deterministic diagnostics, Jev triage, suggestions, the monitor's own consumption and linked E2E executions, or null. A completed analysi\n\"github::issue::close\" :: Close an issue, optionally with a closing comment and a completed / not-planned reason.\n\"github::release::create\" :: Create a GitHub release for a tag, optionally as a draft or prerelease. generate_notes autogenerates notes from merged PRs.\n\"harness::ask\" :: Ask the user for a decision between discrete options: 1-4 questions, 2-4 options each; the UI adds a free-text \"Other\" choice, so do not include one. The questions are shown as a cli\n\"harness::metrics\" :: Aggregate durable model usage, function outcomes, and available trace/span observability for the session tree `root_session_id` belongs to (`session_id` is accepted as an alias, \n\"judge::mentions::resolve\" :: Resolve @<name>(id=\"…\") chat mentions (found in `text`, or listed) through the workers that provide them: each one's status, one-line summary and the call that returns it\n\"memory::preview\" :: Preview the memory injection for a hypothetical chat message: the exact system-prompt memory section a new session gets (rules, budgets, truncation markers; running sessions recei\n\"memory::recall\" :: Search a bank's memories relevant to a query (BM25 + entities + corroboration + recency; no LLM). The same scorer the pre-generate hook uses; the hook injects only the hits with ev\n\"provider::openai::image::generate\" :: Generate one image from a text prompt with gpt-image-2.5-sunburst or gpt-image-2.5-flare (OpenAI Images API, router-resolved credential). Returns viewable conten\n\"provider::openai::image::read\" :: Read back an image saved by image::generate (its details.path or bare file name under data/provider-openai/images/) as viewable content blocks: a JPEG preview (defau\n\"router::models::list\" :: List catalog models, optionally filtered by provider, a capability flag, and modality (chat by default; stt, tts, or any).\n\"router::provider::list\" :: List registered providers with their configured/available status, where each credential comes from (credential_source, credential_ref, credential_error; never a value), and\n\"session::messages-tail\" :: Newest page of the active path, walking backwards in block-aligned pages (a tool run never splits) with activity runs collapsed to placeholders; the reader a chat UI opens \n\"shell::exec_bg\" :: Spawn a background job; returns { job_id, argv } immediately. Accepts the shell::exec payload plus optional job_id. Register shell::job-finished with a fresh job_id before calling \n\"shell::list\" :: List background jobs (running + recently completed). Takes no arguments.\n\"workflow::inject-guidance\" :: Internal pre_generate hook: appends workflow orchestration guidance to the agent system prompt. Bound to harness::hook::pre-generate at worker startup; not called direct\n\"workflow::wake\" :: Internal: on a harness turn-completed event, wake the owning run with a tick. Best-effort latency optimization; the cron sweep is the durable backstop. Not called directly.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"24c6eb84-2154-4027-9b55-149740a